From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <imeri@lanth.me>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] composefs: Replace a staged UKI's boot entries instead of
 adding to them

Staging a UKI deployment wrote its entries into loader/entries.staged
next to whatever an earlier staged deployment left there. The entry's
file name carries the version, so staging a newer image over a staged
one of another version kept the old entry. Status then listed that
deployment without counting it as staged or rollback, garbage
collection dropped its image's tag and objects while its entry and
state stayed, and every later status failed to open its manifest.

Remove the staged entries before writing the new ones, as Type 1
entries for a kernel and initrd already do.
---
 crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/boot.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/boot.rs b/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/boot.rs
index e8aa73f..818f24e 100644
--- a/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/boot.rs
+++ b/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/boot.rs
@@ -1897,6 +1897,9 @@ fn write_systemd_uki_config(
         }
 
         BootSetupType::Upgrade((_, booted_cfs, ..)) => {
+            esp_dir
+                .remove_all_optional(TYPE1_ENT_PATH_STAGED)
+                .with_context(|| format!("Removing {TYPE1_ENT_PATH_STAGED}"))?;
             esp_dir
                 .create_dir_all(TYPE1_ENT_PATH_STAGED)
                 .with_context(|| format!("Creating {TYPE1_ENT_PATH_STAGED}"))?;
-- 
